46],"logprob":-0.11146537214517593,"token":"."}],"message":{"content":"Echo State Networks (ESNs) are a type of recurrent neural network used for processing time-series data. They consist of a large, sparsely connected hidden layer called the \"reservoir,\" which processes input data. The weights of the reservoir are typically fixed and randomly assigned, and only the output weights are trained. Training involves adjusting the output weights to map the reservoir's dynamics to the desired output.\n\nReservoirs in ESNs are trained by adjusting the output weights, not the reservoir itself, which remains fixed. This makes the training process much faster and more efficient compared to training a fully connected recurrent neural network.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":1060,"prompt_eval_duration":44597000,"total_duration":1716848300}}